  "body": "## Issue\nRefs #628 (umbrella of the UX survey); follow-up of #668 (spec of #633)\nDirect-PR: PO decision of 2026-11-09, recorded after #668 was merged\n\n## What and why\nThe PO chose Tailscale Funnel for the survey's public exposure: respondents open a public `https` address without installing anything, only the VPS runs Tailscale, and the other application on the host stays private. #668 was merged with the choice still open; this PR records it in `docs/ux/questionnaire/formulaire-spec.md`:\n- Funnel is the retained option (§11); the reverse proxy stays as a fallback only if the client-IP check of §13 fails;\n- final removal starts by turning Funnel off for the port;\n- §13 drops the open choice and keeps the checks to run on the host (client-IP header forwarded by Funnel, what `tailscaled` logs); the data notice (#669) already names the Tailscale relay.\n\n## How it was verified\n- `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1` with the repository config: 0 errors.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (docs only)\n- [x] Tests added/updated: not applicable, docs only\n- [x] No secrets; fixtures anonymized\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] Author model: Opus 5.5 / Reviewer: the PO\n- [x] Fixes or changes a legacy-app behaviour? No\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified that Tailscale Funnel is the selected option for public access and does not require opening public ports.\n  * Documented the reverse proxy as a fallback if verification fails, with the subdomain and DNS setup applying only when that fallback is used.\n  * Added checks for client address handling and Tailscale logs, and clarified how to disable Funnel or remove the fallback proxy and DNS entry.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
